# Investment Process — Start Here

This folder is the brain of your Stock Research Agent. The agent reads these notes live every time it runs, so they define how it thinks. Right now they hold **default frameworks** as placeholders. The agent will work immediately, but it is generic until you make these notes yours.

## How to make it yours

Go note by note. Each one has a short explanation, a default framework the agent falls back on, and clearly marked `> FILL THIS IN` prompts. Replace the defaults with how *you* actually invest. Anything you write outranks the agent's generic priors and gets tagged `[vault]` in its output. Anything you leave blank gets tagged `[default]` and listed in a "Gaps" section, so the agent literally hands you your own to-do list.

Highest-leverage notes to fill first: **Philosophy**, **Checklist** (your hard disqualifiers), and **Cognitive Biases** (the ones you know you fall for). Those three change the agent's verdicts the most.

## The notes

- **Philosophy.md**: what you want to own and why; your edge; your circle of competence
- **Moat Analysis.md**: how you judge competitive advantage and its durability
- **Cognitive Biases.md**: your personal failure modes and how to catch them
- **Portfolio Strategy.md**: construction, concentration limits, position sizing
- **Thesis Template.md**: what a complete thesis looks like for you
- **Checklist.md**: pre-investment checklist and hard disqualifiers (fast kills)
- **Sell Discipline.md**: when you sell, trim, or hold
- **Holdings.md**: your current book (needed for fit checks and re-tests)
- **Theses/**: one note per position you hold
- **Watchlist/**: ideas under consideration
- **Fit Checks/**: where portfolio-fit notes get written

## The four workflows

Ask in plain language:

- "stress test my thesis on TICKER" → pressure-test a held position
- "first pass on TICKER" → triage a new idea
- "does TICKER fit my portfolio" → fit check before adding
- "re-test my TICKER thesis after earnings" / "audit my TICKER thesis for bias" → maintenance loop

The agent writes a dated, Dataview-queryable note back here for every run, building a research trail you can re-test against.
